From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FormalSnake <kyaniserni@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:47:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpui_linux: take window focus from xdg_toplevel activated

A toplevel's focus follows the activated state of its configure, the
compositor's own statement. Keyboard enter and leave only route keys, so
a virtual keyboard coming and going (wtype, an on-screen keyboard) keeps
the focus, and focus moving to another client with no keyboard present
still ends it. Popups and layer surfaces, which have no activated state,
keep taking focus from the keyboard.

A keyboard that leaves or is removed releases the keys it delivered,
resets modifiers and ends its composition, also while a blocking child
window or a nested event loop holds the window's input. The client
follows one seat: events from other seats are ignored, and removing the
followed seat ends its devices' input and moves to the next seat.
---
